From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DPP: clamp the chirp wait time to the driver limit

wpas_dpp_chirp_start() sends each Presence Announcement with a wait time
of 2000 ms. cfg80211 refuses a frame whose wait exceeds the driver's
maximum remain-on-channel duration with -EINVAL (nl80211_tx_mgmt()), so
on a driver with a smaller maximum, such as mac80211_hwsim with 1000 ms,
no chirp is ever transmitted and the enrollee cannot be found.

Clamp the wait time to max_remain_on_chan, as the other DPP transmit
paths in this file do.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
@@ -5143,6 +5143,7 @@ static void wpas_dpp_chirp_tx_status(str
 static void wpas_dpp_chirp_start(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s)
 {
 	struct wpabuf *msg, *announce = NULL;
+	unsigned int wait_time;
 	int type;
 
 	msg = wpa_s->dpp_presence_announcement;
@@ -5166,6 +5167,9 @@ static void wpas_dpp_chirp_start(struct
 			return;
 		type = DPP_PA_RECONFIG_ANNOUNCEMENT;
 	}
+	wait_time = wpa_s->max_remain_on_chan;
+	if (wait_time > 2000)
+		wait_time = 2000;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "DPP: Chirp on %d MHz", wpa_s->dpp_chirp_freq);
 	wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_INFO, DPP_EVENT_TX "dst=" MACSTR " freq=%u type=%d",
 		MAC2STR(broadcast), wpa_s->dpp_chirp_freq, type);
@@ -5173,7 +5177,7 @@ static void wpas_dpp_chirp_start(struct
 		    wpa_s, wpa_s->dpp_chirp_freq, broadcast,
 		    wpa_s->own_addr, broadcast,
 		    wpabuf_head(msg), wpabuf_len(msg),
-		    2000, wpas_dpp_chirp_tx_status, 0) < 0)
+		    wait_time, wpas_dpp_chirp_tx_status, 0) < 0)
 		wpas_dpp_chirp_tx_status(wpa_s, wpa_s->dpp_chirp_freq,
 					 broadcast, wpa_s->own_addr, broadcast,
 					 wpabuf_head(msg), wpabuf_len(msg),
